@startuml
title MusicHub - Resource Owner Password Credentials

actor "Resource owner\nalumno.demo" as Owner
participant "Legacy client\nlegacy-client" as Client
participant "Authorization server\n/oauth/token" as Auth
participant "Resource server\n/api" as Resource
database "MusicHub database" as DB

Owner -> Client: Provides username and password
Client -> Auth: POST /oauth/token\ngrant_type=password\nclient_id + client_secret\nscope=profile.read playlists.read
Auth -> DB: Load client, user and allowed scopes
DB --> Auth: Hashed password, client secret hash and scopes
Auth -> Auth: Validate grant, client secret,\nuser password and requested scopes
Auth -> Auth: Sign JWT with iss, sub, aud,\niat, exp, jti, client_id, scope
Auth --> Client: 200 access_token, token_type,\nexpires_in, scope

Client -> Resource: GET /api/me\nAuthorization: Bearer access_token
Resource -> Resource: Verify JWT signature,\nissuer, audience, exp and profile.read
Resource -> DB: Load profile for token subject
DB --> Resource: User profile
Resource --> Client: 200 profile

Client -> Resource: GET /api/playlists\nAuthorization: Bearer access_token
Resource -> Resource: Verify playlists.read scope
Resource -> DB: Load playlists for token subject
DB --> Resource: Authorized playlists
Resource --> Client: 200 playlists

note over Owner,Client
ROPC is included only as a legacy lab flow.
The client handles the password, so it is not recommended
for new applications.
end note
@enduml
